# Endpoint credentials for OpenClaw. Provide ONE of the two keys below
# (or both — your OpenRouter key is used first when both are set).
#
# Easiest path: set these as Codespaces secrets (the Codespace prompts you on
# creation). Then you can ignore this file.
#
# Otherwise, run `bash scripts/set-key.sh` and it will be written for you to
# ~/.openclaw/.env — do NOT commit your real key.

# COURSE STANDARD: your OWN OpenRouter key (starts with sk-or-). $20 in
# OpenRouter credits is a required course material for Fall 2026. Create the
# account and key at https://openrouter.ai (Settings -> Keys). Do NOT enable
# auto top-up. Used first whenever it is set. Default model:
# google/gemini-3.7-flash, with qwen/qwen3.7-flash as the cheap fallback.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-REPLACE_ME

# NO-COST ALTERNATIVE: OU AI Sandbox key (starts with sk-), issued by the
# course on request. Fully supported; used when no OpenRouter key is set.
# If the $20 is a barrier for you, use this instead and tell the instructor.
#LITELLM_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_ME

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SHIP DAY (research → store → show). Two free accounts, three secrets,
# no credit card, no database service. Set these as Codespaces secrets —
# do NOT commit real values. Full details: shipday/.env.example
# Tavily (web search):  https://tavily.com  → Get API Key  (1,000 free credits/mo)
#TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-REPLACE_ME
# Netlify (deploys your site): User settings → Applications → Personal access token
#NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME
# Netlify (which project to deploy to): from `netlify sites:create` output
#NETLIFY_SITE_ID=REPLACE_ME

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# YOUR CAPSTONE'S OWN SERVICES. Building with live external tools is encouraged.
# When your project needs a service not listed above — a vector store, a maps or
# weather API, an email/SMS sender, another host — follow the same pattern:
#   1. Create the key at the provider (prefer a free tier; set a spend limit).
#   2. Add it as a Codespaces secret at https://github.com/settings/codespaces,
#      grant this repo access, then restart your Codespace so it loads.
#   3. Read it in code with os.environ["YOUR_KEY_NAME"]; never commit real values.
# Ask in class if you are unsure whether a service is a good fit for your scope.
